From: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sprd: stop the DSP when the fast scene stops

scene_fast_trigger() sends SND_VBC_DSP_FUNC_HW_TRIGGER with up_down=1
when the trigger refcount reaches one, and on the way down it only
decrements the refcount. The DSP is never told to stop until the stream
is closed and scene_fast_shutdown() runs.

For this scene the DSP owns the read side of the MCDT fifo and keeps
draining it until it is told otherwise, so that gap is audible. A player
that pauses or is killed leaves the PCM open in SETUP - PipeWire holds
the device for its suspend timeout, which is seconds - and for all of it
the DSP is pulling from a fifo the AP has stopped filling. It replays
whatever stale samples are left as a continuous square-wave buzz.

The firmware is not missing anything here: up_down is a parameter of
SND_VBC_DSP_FUNC_HW_TRIGGER, so the stop half of the pair is part of the
command, and vbc_dsp_func_trigger() reaches it with
aud_send_cmd_no_wait(), which is safe from the atomic trigger path the
start already uses. Send it when the refcount reaches zero.

Only the fast scene is changed. It is the one this board plays through,
and the others carry no exposure here.

Signed-off-by: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/vbc-dai.c b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/vbc-dai.c
index cd4e6be7c240..39f10bd00581 100755
--- a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/vbc-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/vbc-dai.c
@@ -8353,8 +8353,20 @@ static int scene_fast_trigger(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, int cmd,
 
 		trigger_unlock_spin(scene_id, stream);
 	} else {
+		/*
+		 * The DSP owns the MCDT read side for this scene and keeps
+		 * draining it until it is told to stop. Without a matching
+		 * down trigger it runs on past every STOP - PipeWire drops the
+		 * stream but holds the PCM open, so the DSP starves on an
+		 * empty FIFO and replays stale samples as a continuous buzz
+		 * until the suspend timeout finally closes the device.
+		 * SND_VBC_DSP_FUNC_HW_TRIGGER takes up_down as a parameter, so
+		 * the firmware already expects this half of the pair.
+		 */
 		trigger_lock_spin(scene_id, stream);
 		trigger_dec_ref(scene_id, stream);
+		if (trigger_get_ref(scene_id, stream) == 0)
+			ret = dsp_trigger(vbc_codec, scene_id, stream, up_down);
 		trigger_unlock_spin(scene_id, stream);
 	}
 
